39. Decrypting a secret message (Capture-the-Flag, Reverse Engineering)
The task is to decrypt a secret message
The software used for encrypting the secret message is uncovered: See SuperEncrypt.py
So, our task is to attempt to decrypt the secret message in the file Ultra_encrypted_message.txt
What we know:
• The algorithm is based on “clever” use of hashes and hmac
• It even includes a counter scheme
• The designers were not cryptographers and may have made some serious mistakes
• The scheme is also key-less (an amazing feat!)
There is a small prize to be won for the first one (ones, max 2 persons) to decrypt the secret message.
Instructions for how to claim the prize are contained in the encrypted text.